  "asset_audit_2026_08_04": "Tile and Pure image slugs replaced from the Multipanel asset handoff, then every file was fetched and looked at. Ten of the fourteen are room photography rather than isolated swatches, and one (crystal-marble-large) carries a NEW marketing roundel - so swatch_asset is true for only three. That flag is what stops the hero compositor tiling an image across a shower wall, so it is set from what the file actually shows, not from the filename or the handoff summary. Every URL returns HTTP 200 with distinct bytes; the previous data had Tile and Pure pointing at the same files as each other, which these fix regardless."
